# EXPECTATION FOR LANE RUN 25 — derived and committed ALONE, BEFORE the run (D0A-R21-07).
#
# Target commit: a07c21d. Run 24 was attempted and REFUSED; its numbers are not a baseline.
#
# =========================================================================================
# THE DERIVATION — UNCHANGED FROM RUN 24, and that is checkable rather than assumed
# =========================================================================================
#
#   EXECUTED 224 / SKIPPED 8 / reported 232
#
# **No test identity has been added or removed since the run-24 expectation (ecfffec)** —
# enumerated from the diff with `fn [a-z0-9_]+`, both directions, empty. The intervening
# commits fixed a fixture, added an assertion to an existing test, and changed the verifier;
# none of that moves the set. The unprivileged pair is still 204/28/232.
#
# **Run 24 measured 222/8/230 against this same prediction, and the miss was NOT in the
# derivation:** §4b counted 232 identities at root and 232 unprivileged, zero in either
# direction, with exactly the 8 predicted skips. `EXECUTED` counts PASSING tests, so
# 232 − 8 skipped − 2 failed = 222. A match this time therefore confirms the set a second time;
# a repeat of 222 would mean the same two tests failed again, which is the point of the run.
#
# =========================================================================================
# RUN 25 OWES THREE THINGS
# =========================================================================================
#
# 1. **The repeat that distinguishes intermittent from persistent** on run 24's two PAM
#    failures. This is the run's primary obligation.
# 2. **The negative control with a fixture that can be found.** It has EXECUTED EXACTLY ONCE
#    (run 24) and produced no verdict about the assembly — `Unresolved`, because `exec`
#    replaces `comm` and the probe was looking for a name the process no longer had. The
#    fixture now execs a file staged under the SAME name.
# 3. **A fourth positive control**, which proves nothing on its own — see below.
#
# =========================================================================================
# WHAT A CLEAN REPEAT MEANS, AND WHAT A SECOND FAILURE MEANS — fixed before the run
# =========================================================================================
#
# Run 24's failures were `b1_token_expiry_blocks_the_assembled_loop` (ShellSetupFailed) and
# `the_daemon_binary_runs_the_real_gate_d0a_r4_03` (pam_open_session failed). Runs 20, 21 and
# 23 had zero failures. They are attributable to NEITHER my changes NOR §6's documented
# parallel-PAM artifact (measured 0/30 serial; run 24 was serial).
#
# 1. **BOTH PASS -> INTERMITTENT, and still UNEXPLAINED.** One clean repeat does not identify a
#    cause; it bounds the frequency at "not every run". The honest record is *intermittent,
#    cause unknown*, and §6's own rule then applies: a test whose outcome varies needs >=30
#    iterations before its green is evidence. **A clean repeat does NOT close this** — it
#    changes what is owed from "diagnose a persistent failure" to "measure an intermittent one".
#
# 2. **EITHER FAILS AGAIN -> PERSISTENT, and a genuine finding about the assembly.** Two
#    consecutive serial runs failing the same PAM path is not contention this project has
#    measured away, and the "harness" explanation would then be dead by evidence rather than by
#    assertion. That is a product-side investigation, and it outranks everything else in the
#    arc — the daemon's shell setup failing at root is the trust boundary's own path.
#
# 3. **DIFFERENT TESTS FAIL -> a third case, named so it is not folded into the first two.**
#    That would suggest an environmental variable neither run controls (session pressure, a
#    leftover logind session, resource limits) and makes the environment itself the subject.
#
# Whichever occurs, it is recorded as the case it is. Reconstructing the reading afterwards is
# what this project has paid for repeatedly.
#
# =========================================================================================
# A FOURTH `Reached` STILL PROVES NOTHING ON ITS OWN
# =========================================================================================
#
# This was stated in run 24's expectation and it held: the positive control returned `Reached`
# for a fourth time (runs 20, 21, 23, 24) and it changed nothing. **The negative control is the
# only thing that gives the positives meaning, and it has produced no verdict about the assembly
# in its single execution.** Three prior `Reached` verdicts plus a fourth remain consistent with
# a control that has never discriminated.
#
# If the negative control returns `Topology` this run, that changes retrospectively — the
# positives become reports from an instrument shown to discriminate. If it returns `Reached`,
# the supplementary scan is WITHDRAWN from D0A-R28-02's row entirely rather than weakened. If it
# returns `Scan`/`Unresolved` a second time, the fixture is wrong twice and the right move is to
# stop building fixtures and ask whether the probe should identify the AI by PROVENANCE rather
# than by name — which is where R34-01's lesson pointed and I did not follow it far enough.
#
# =========================================================================================
# ACCEPTANCE
# =========================================================================================
#
# `scripts/lane-accept.py scratch/lane-run-25` decides. It now requires the negative control's
# evidence with a `Topology` verdict, so **a run whose negative control returns anything else is
# refused** — including the outcome that would be a genuine product finding. That is deliberate:
# the lane's evidence would not support the closure it is cited for.
#
# The commit binding is captured in `hygiene.txt`, with the run's own artifact directory
# filtered from the dirty check — a false positive that would have refused every future run and
# was caught on the tool's SECOND use, by the tool being used rather than by someone reading.
EXPECTED_EXECUTED=224
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=8
EXPECTED_REPORTED=232
